<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Central Bank sells dollar-indexed notes.</title>
<headline>Brazil Central Bank sells dollar-indexed notes.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank sold Monday 500 million reais of special dollar-indexed Central Bank Notes (NBC-E), dealers said.</p>
<p>The notes, which have a six-month maturity and expire on August 25, 1997, will pay an annual yield of 11.39 percent plus the variation of the foreign exchange rate in the period, they added.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5418))</p>
